### Vulnerability: Unchecked Payment Receiver
### Explanation: The contract uses Gtxn[1].amount() to deduct funds from global state but doesn't verify that transaction 1 is actually sending funds to the intended recipient, allowing attackers to redirect payments to arbitrary addresses while still passing contract checks.
### Risk: Critical - Complete loss of funds as attackers can redirect all distributed payments to their own addresses.
